Slot 012 is spent, not free.

012_local_tree_roots_follow_current.sql pointed local-tree source roots at
the cache's `current` link. It lifted the managed_sources_immutable trigger
around the rewrite with ALTER TABLE ... DISABLE TRIGGER, and that trigger is
declarative state (managed_sources.sql) first shipped in 0.53 -- a database
last booted on 0.52.0 does not have it, and the migration failed every
upgrade at "trigger managed_sources_immutable does not exist".

The rewrite moved to 013_local_tree_roots_follow_current.sql, which lifts
the trigger only where it exists. Deployments that applied 012 keep their
tracking row; 013 is a no-op for them.

Numbering continues at the highest slot ever used, never at the first gap.
